gold: restore the linear lmbda schedule

Applies to: github.com/laminair/gb-steps-distillation at a5d59bc4 -- the commit this
            step's code_config pins -- from the checkout ROOT (paths are the repo's own):

              git -C <checkout> apply steps/distill/gold/skypilot/patches/lmbda_linear_schedule.diff

            git apply skips this header. Upstream HEAD 59c36a2 has the same defect.

THE DEFECT. _get_current_lmbda() handles only "constant". Its "linear" branch sits after
the `return` of _draw_on_policy, the method inserted above it when the on-policy draw was
made rank-consistent, so the branch is unreachable. With lmbda_schedule linear the method
returns None, and draw_on_policy() raises TypeError on `None <= 0.0` at the first training
step, after the allocation is already held. render_gold_config.py accepts linear, because
the CONFIG is valid; it is the trainer that cannot run it.

THE FIX moves those 12 lines back into _get_current_lmbda, unchanged. The constant path is
untouched, so a constant-lmbda run on the patched checkout trains exactly as on the pin.
Verified 2026-10-05 by exercising the method on a stub: lmbda_init 0.25 to lmbda 0.5 over
max_steps 2,500 gives 0.25 / 0.3125 / 0.375 / 0.4375 / 0.5 at steps 0 / 625 / 1250 /
1875 / 2500, and constant returns lmbda.

A REPRODUCIBLE COMMIT. With this identity and date, and UNSIGNED, the patched commit is
288bfc6bdab589eca394ca9f7229f1138a6da1c4 on any machine, which is what lets a recipe pin
it as CODE_EXPECT_REF before the checkout exists. A signature is part of the commit
object, so a machine that signs by default (commit.gpgsign) gets a different hash
without the -c below:

  git clone https://github.com/laminair/gb-steps-distillation.git <checkout>
  git -C <checkout> checkout a5d59bc45524a8d75706e20d44ae1a254f273f23
  git -C <checkout> apply <this file>
  GIT_AUTHOR_NAME=granite.build GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL=granite.build@localhost \
  GIT_COMMITTER_NAME=granite.build GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL=granite.build@localhost \
  GIT_AUTHOR_DATE=2026-10-05T00:00:00+0000 GIT_COMMITTER_DATE=2026-10-05T00:00:00+0000 \
    git -C <checkout> -c commit.gpgsign=false commit -qam "gold: restore the linear lmbda schedule"

